gaps=[{'id':'L34-G01','physicalPages':[1038,1039,1043,1044,1046,1047],'angle':'Full multilayer forward/loss/backward/update synthesis','finding':'The134 items separately test a hidden forward map, output sigmoid, scalar linear gradient and nonlinear derivative factor, but never perform one complete multilayer gradient/update chain. The actual training-stage diagram and chain-rule content support a meaningful hard synthesis.','boundedRemedy':'Provide a small nondegenerate two-layer network, explicit column shapes, biases, one target, loss and rate. Compute hidden/output values, loss, output and hidden gradients, and simultaneous parameter updates. Keep ReLU inputs away from zero or declare its convention. Cite all affine, activation, loss and chain-rule premises; independently execute finite-difference checks.'},{'id':'L34-G02','physicalPages':[1032,1033],'angle':'Multi-example perceptron trace with both mistake branches','finding':'Current trace questions cover one positive update and negative equality, not a sequence that distinguishes update timing, bias changes, correct-example no-ops and revisiting.','boundedRemedy':'Supply a finite separable set, explicit augmented coordinates, initial weights and deterministic presentation order as a variation of the random-choice source. Trace both positive and negative mistakes plus at least one correct example, and check all-example termination. Do not infer a single-pass convergence guarantee.'},{'id':'L34-G03','physicalPages':[1043],'angle':'Negative-label and batch binary cross-entropy','finding':'The only numerical binary loss item uses y1,p0.5. It does not test the(1-y)log(1-p) branch or averaging over mixed labels, despite those being explicit terms in the source formula.','boundedRemedy':'Supply at least one positive and one negative target with predicted class1 probabilities, use the explicitly repaired negative mean log-likelihood, and calculate both per-example terms and their average. Compare sign, class-probability and sum-versus-mean mistakes with natural-log and exact/rounded conventions.'},{'id':'L34-G04','physicalPages':[1025,1028],'angle':'Named MP versus trainable-perceptron historical attribution','finding':'The source explicitly attributes the1943 artificial-neuron model to McCulloch/Pitts, including their complementary disciplines, and the1958 classical perceptron to Rosenblatt. Existing questions address Minsky/Papert misattribution and broad timeline associations, but not this direct model/person distinction.','boundedRemedy':'Add one narrow source-attributed matching/statement item connecting the two named models, contributors and fixed-logic versus learnable-parameter distinction. Avoid repeating unreliable robotics dates or adding an unsupported invention claim.'}]
